\subsection{Video JDS model for SmartEye}


\begin{itemize}

\item Compared to glasses JDS algorithm, some variables can not be measured accurately form video signals. Any variable associated with DOQ, Saccades, Long Closures are not available for video data. The following variables are used in the linear model:

<<independent_var, cache=TRUE, echo=FALSE>>=

   indep_var <- c("LnMeanPositiveZCI",
                  "LnStdDevPositiveZCI",
                  "LnMeanNegativeZCI" ,
                  "LnStdDevNegativeZCI", 
                  "LnMeanNegativeIED", 
                  "LnStdDevNegativeIED",     
                  "LnMeanBECD",
                  "LnStdDevBECD",
                  "LnMeanBTD",
                  "LnStdDevBTD",
                  "LnMeanPositiveAVR",
                  "LnStdDevPositiveAVR",
                  "LnMeanNegativeAVR",
                  "LnStdDevNegativeAVR", 
                  "LnMeanAVRProduct", 
                  "LnStdDevAVRProduct")
   
@


<<var_print, cache=TRUE, echo= FALSE, results='text'>>=

   print(indep_var)
@



\item The same difinition/criteria are used to define blink\_correct\_shape for both glasses and video blinks. These criteria are defined based on glasses blinks characteristics.

%\end{itemize}


%To develop new weightings for video JDS model, two appproaches are used:

%\begin{itemize}
\item Linear model: Since there is no data associated with driving condition, the component identified by JDSB is irrelevent here. The Raw JDS is nothing but the JDSA itself. JDSA is fitted using stepwise forward-backward variable selection method. 

%\item Logistic model: using the original class labels of alert and drowsy minutes, a model is build to predict the probability of being in a class. 

\end{itemize}




<<linear_regression_data_prep, cache=TRUE ,echo=FALSE>>=

#Store summary stat from samrtEye
sm_ss <- list()

# store jds score from glasses 
   
gl_score <- list()

# Read summary  stat file
for(s in 1:length(sm_session_final))
{
  ss <- read.csv(list.files(paste0(sm_session_final[s],"/smarteye"), pattern = "summary_stats.csv", full.names = TRUE)
                        , header=TRUE, stringsAsFactors = FALSE, check.names = FALSE)
  ss$device <- "SmartEye"
  ss$session <- basename(sm_session_final[s])
  sm_ss[[s]] <- ss
  
  # read score file from glasses
  gl <- read.csv(list.files(paste0(sm_session_final[s],"/glasses"), pattern = "jds_stats.csv", full.names = TRUE)
                        , header=TRUE, stringsAsFactors = FALSE, check.names = FALSE)
  gl$device <- "Glasses"
  gl$session <- basename(sm_session_final[s])
  gl_score[[s]] <- gl
  
}


# combine data for all sessions 
sm_mdt <- do.call(rbind, sm_ss)
############## add JTV responses ##############
sm_mdt <- right_join(sm_mdt, sm_jtv_all[,c("session","JTV_percentage_20min")], by="session")


############## add  n_lapses responses ##############
sm_mdt <- right_join(sm_mdt, sm_jtv_pm_lapsing_all[,c("session","window", "n_stimuli", "n_lapses")], by=c("session", "window"))


############################## add state : impaired ( JTV_percentage_20min > 5%) ######################
sm_mdt$state20min <- "not_impaired"
sm_mdt$state20min[sm_mdt$JTV_percentage_20min > 5] <- "impaired"
sm_mdt$state20min <- factor(sm_mdt$state20min , levels= c("not_impaired","impaired"))



############################## add lapsing minute ( n_lapses > 0) ######################
sm_mdt$lapsing_minute <- "no"
sm_mdt$lapsing_minute[sm_mdt$n_lapses > 0] <- "yes"
sm_mdt$lapsing_minute <- factor(sm_mdt$lapsing_minute , levels= c("no","yes"))


# remove NA
sm_mdt <- na.omit(sm_mdt)


#########################  glasses ######################
# combined glasses score for all sessions
# for a valid comparison to video model, raw jds are truncated to 0, 10
gl_score_all <- do.call(rbind, gl_score)

gl_score_all <- right_join(gl_score_all, sm_jtv_all[,c("session","JTV_percentage_20min")], by="session")
gl_score_all <-  right_join(gl_score_all , sm_jtv_pm_lapsing_all[,c("session","window", "n_stimuli", "n_lapses")], by=c("session", "window"))

gl_score_all$state20min <- "not_impaired"
gl_score_all$state20min[gl_score_all$JTV_percentage_20min > 5] <- "impaired"
gl_score_all$state20min <- factor(gl_score_all$state20min , levels= c("not_impaired","impaired"))

gl_score_all$lapsing_minute <- "no"
gl_score_all$lapsing_minute[gl_score_all$n_lapses > 0] <- "yes"
gl_score_all$lapsing_minute <- factor(gl_score_all$lapsing_minute , levels= c("no","yes"))

gl_score_all <- na.omit(gl_score_all)

@



%\clearpage

\subsection[Linear model: SmartEye video]{Video JDS model for SmartEye using JTV\_percentage\_20min as state of impairment}

A video model is derived using the per minute observations. The JTV\_percentage\_20min is used to define the state of impairment. Every valid minute in a recording is labelled as  not\_impaired if the JTV\_percetage\_20min is below $5\%$ and impaired otherwise. 

To facilitate the linear model, all the not\_impaired observaitons are coded as -4 and al lthe impaired observaions are coded as 9. Important variables are selected using the stepwsie forward-backward algorithm. 



<<linear_jds, cache=TRUE, echo= FALSE, warning=FALSE, message=FALSE>>=

# jds code: alert = -1 and drowsy = 8
sm_mdt$state20min_code <- -4
sm_mdt$state20min_code[sm_mdt$state20min =="impaired"] <- 9

####################### forward- backward variable selection ###################
# jds original model formula
state20min_imf <- formula(paste0('state20min_code',"~", paste0(indep_var, collapse = "+")))

# jdsa full model
state20min_full_mod <- ols(state20min_imf, data= sm_mdt)

# extract dependent variable from formula
state20min_dep_var <- all.vars(update(state20min_imf,.~0))

# check if there is multicollinearity issue/ offending variables exits. 
# The offending variables coeffcients are not estimating and dropped from analysis
  if(any(is.na(state20min_full_mod$coefficients))==TRUE){
    # model with non-offending  predictors
    state20min_imf_new <- formula(paste0(state20min_dep_var, "~", 
                                         paste0(names(state20min_full_mod$coefficients[!is.na(state20min_full_mod$coefficients)])[-1], collapse="+")))
    # fit new full model after dropping offending variables 
    state20min_full_mod_new <- ols(state20min_imf_new, data=sm_mdt) 
  } else{
  # if no offending variables exists use the full.mod
    state20min_imf_new <- state20min_imf
    state20min_full_mod_new <- state20min_full_mod
  }
  # Perform backward elimination for model persimony	
  state20min_step_mod <- fastbw(state20min_full_mod_new, rule='p', type='individual', sls=0.05) 
  # final model formula
  state20min_imf_final <- formula(paste0(state20min_dep_var, "~", paste0(state20min_step_mod$names.kept, collapse="+")))
  # final model after variable selection /backward elimination
  state20min_final_mod <- ols(state20min_imf_final, data=sm_mdt)

@


The final model selected for JDS using forward-backward variable elimination is  

<<state20min_final_model_print, cache=TRUE ,echo=FALSE, results='text'>>=

  print(state20min_final_mod)
  
@


Raw JDS values are obtained by multiplying the weights with the corresponding values of the selected variables. Truncation was done to have all values between $0$ and $10$. 

<<jdsa_calc, cache=TRUE, echo=FALSE, warning=FALSE, message=FALSE>>=

# calculate jds values
sm_mdt$state20min_jds <- predict(state20min_final_mod, data = sm_mdt)  
  
# truncate to have values in between 0 (values <0 to 0) and 10 (values > 10 to 10)
sm_mdt$state20min_jds[sm_mdt$state20min_jds <= 0] <- 0
sm_mdt$state20min_jds[sm_mdt$state20min_jds >= 10] <- 10

# write.csv(sm_mdt, "C:/Research/VideoReport_YK/SmartEye_everything/JDSModel_New/smarteye_new_jds_model_2.csv", row.names=FALSE)

@




